## Money gates (paper → real capital)

These gates are the **only** path from idea to capital. No exceptions, no shortcuts.

- **Backtest → paper:** strategy shows positive expectancy **net of the full cost model** over
  a multi-year backtest with CPCV-style validation (not a single random split). Deflated Sharpe
  reported alongside raw Sharpe.

- **Paper → small live:** **60 consecutive paper-trading days at ≥ 1.0 Sharpe net of all costs.**
  If this gate takes longer than expected — good. More data.

- **Small live → scale:** **3 months live at ≥ 0.7× the paper Sharpe.** 30%+ live-vs-paper
  shrinkage is normal; materially worse means a leak — go back, don't size up.

