## The confidence engine — how every alert is scored

This is the core of the system. The confidence number is not picked — it is computed through
nine independent layers. Each layer is independent. Independent confirmations multiply confidence
rather than adding it: six independent forces pointing the same direction simultaneously is not
coincidence — it is institutional intent.

```
Layer 0:  Hard gates          (binary kills — any failure = silent discard)
Layer 1:  Market regime       (−30 to +30)
Layer 2:  Sector alignment    (−15 to +15)
Layer 3:  Fundamental quality (−20 to +20)
Layer 4:  Technical alignment (−20 to +30)
Layer 5:  Signal-specific     (0 to +20)
Layer 6:  Confluence bonus    (0 to +20)
Layer 7:  Psychological state (−20 to +15)
Layer 8:  Institutional       (−10 to +15)
Layer 9:  Event proximity     (−15 to +10)

→ Normalised to 0–1
→ Thresholds: 0.55 (send) / 0.65 (good) / 0.75 (strong) / 0.85 (exceptional)
```

**Layer 0 — Hard gates (any one kills the signal):**
- Stock in blacklist (GSM/ASM/Unsolicited)
- Stock in F&O ban
- Newly listed < 30 days
- Promoter pledge > 50%
- Long signal on loss-making company
- Liquidity < ₹5 Cr avg daily turnover
- 09:15–09:30 observation window
- Call auction / T2T segment

**Layer 1 — Market regime** inputs: Nifty direction, VIX level/direction, GIFT Nifty alignment,
FII partial-day flow, advance-decline ratio, % stocks above VWAP, breadth (% above 200d MA).
Expiry effects: aligned with max pain direction = +5, against = −10.

**Layer 2 — Sector alignment** inputs: sector RS rank (1 = best, 11 = worst), RS trend
(improving/flat/deteriorating), sector volume vs 20d avg, global sector parallel
(US sector ETF aligned or diverging).

**Layer 3 — Fundamental quality** inputs: quality score (0–100), revenue growth YoY, earnings
quality (CFO/PAT ratio, receivables/revenue trend), D/E ratio, promoter holding/pledge,
recent rating action (upgrade/downgrade), delivery conviction z-score.

**Layer 4 — Technical alignment** inputs: daily trend regime (5 states), 5-min RSI (healthy
range 50–65 for longs), VWAP side + slope, Bollinger squeeze, volume ratio, proximity to
key levels (PDH/PDL, round numbers, 52w extremes), pattern flags.

**Layer 5 — Signal-specific quality** inputs depend on signal type. OI: OI% change, price%
change, volume confirmation. Breakout: level cleanness, volume. Announcement: surprise magnitude,
sentiment score, earnings quality of the beat.

**Layer 6 — Confluence bonus** fires when multiple independent signals simultaneously confirm
the same stock. OI buildup + volume surge = +0.10. Breakout + result beat = +0.15.
Rating upgrade + technical breakout = +0.12. Smart money + VWAP hold + sector leading = +0.15.

**Layer 7 — Psychological state** from the classifier (see Phase 6). NEUTRAL_TRENDING = +0.05.
FOMO_EUPHORIA with long signal = −0.20 (near-kill). CAPITULATION with long signal = +0.15
(contrarian). SELL_NEWS confirmed with short signal = +0.15. BUY_RUMOR active with long = −0.10.

**Layer 8 — Institutional** inputs: smart money score (0–1), FII derivative positioning
(index puts adding = bearish for macro), block deal tier (Tier-1 institution = +0.10),
participant-wise OI net direction.

**Layer 9 — Event proximity** inputs: days to next event, pre-event run score (stock already
up 10%+ = −0.15 for longs), IV vs 5d avg (elevated IV = uncertainty premium exists),
rumor detection score, post-announcement reaction pattern if event just occurred.

