### New collectors

**`collectors/participant_oi.py`** (EOD ~19:00 IST):
NSE F&O daily reports: FII/DII/Pro/Client × Index Fut/Stock Fut/Index Opt/Stock Opt.
Long contracts, short contracts, net position per category.
→ `raw_participant_oi` table.

Signal: FII adding index put longs = bearish macro. FII adding index call longs = bullish.
Client (retail) net short extreme = contrarian bullish (smart money vs retail).

**`collectors/slb.py`** (daily):
SLB segment data — India's short-interest proxy.
Rising lend rates + volumes = increasing short interest.
Falling lending = short covering → potential short squeeze setup.

**`collectors/fno_ban_list.py`** (EOD):
Stocks above 95% MWPL → F&O ban. Hard exclude from long signals.
Stocks returning from ban (OI falls below 80%) → re-entry opportunity flag.

**`collectors/index_rebalancing.py`** (event-driven, IISL announcements):
Addition to Nifty 50/500/sector → forced passive buying window.
Removal → forced selling window.
Alert fires on announcement day (2 weeks before effective date).

### Smart money score

`smart_money/score.py` (daily, 0–1):
```
FII cash flow today           25% weight
FII derivative positioning    20%
DII activity                  15%
Block deal institutions       15%
Promoter activity             15%
SLB short interest            10%

> 0.70 → accumulation
0.40–0.70 → mixed
< 0.40 → distribution
```

### Block deal institution database

`config/institution_database.yaml`:
Tier-1: LIC, SBI MF, HDFC MF, ICICI Pru MF, Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley, BofA, Citi,
Temasek, GIC Singapore, Norges Bank, CPPIB, Jefferies.
Tier-2: Motilal Oswal, Kotak, Axis MF, regional domestic funds.

Tier-1 block purchase → +0.10 confidence boost.
Tier-1 block sale → context-dependent (rebalancing vs losing confidence).

### Options Greeks and derivatives intelligence (currently entirely missing)

`options/greeks.py` (per option chain poll, every 5 min):
Compute delta/gamma/theta/vega per strike using `mibian` library.
Inputs: spot (from raw_equity_quotes), strike, time-to-expiry, risk-free rate
(10yr G-Sec yield proxy), IV (from NSE-published bid-ask).

**Net dealer gamma (GEX):**
Positive GEX → market makers long gamma → mean-reverting tape (buy dips, sell rallies).
Negative GEX → market makers short gamma → trending tape (momentum works).
This is why some days Nifty oscillates 50 points and others trends 300.

**Max pain per expiry:**
Strike where maximum options expire worthless. On expiry day, price gravitates here.
Alert within 2% of max pain on expiry Tuesday/Thursday → `max_pain_drift` signal.

**PCR extremes already partially collected.** Add ATM PCR (not just total).

**New option signals:**
`pcr_extreme_low` (< 0.7 contrarian bearish), `pcr_extreme_high` (> 1.3 contrarian bullish),
`max_pain_drift`, `gamma_squeeze_risk`, `heavy_ce_writing`, `heavy_pe_writing`, `iv_spike`.

**Index rebalancing signal:**
`index_addition` → buy window of ~2 weeks (forced passive buying).
`index_removal` → avoid longs / potential short.

