### Full 9-layer confidence engine

`confidence_engine.py` implementing all layers from the taxonomy above.
Normalised to 0–1 with thresholds 0.55/0.65/0.75/0.85.

All existing layers (1–4 from Phase 1–2, partially 3 from Phase 4) are formalised here.
New layers 7–9 from Phases 6–7 now integrated.

### Confluence detector

`confluence/detector.py`:
OI buildup + volume surge simultaneously = +0.10.
Breakout + result beat = +0.15.
Rating upgrade + technical breakout = +0.12.
Smart money accumulating + VWAP hold + sector leading = +0.15.
Multiple signal types on same stock within 30 minutes = +0.08.

Rule: independent confirmations multiply confidence, they do not add.
Probability that 6 independent forces all point the wrong direction simultaneously is negligible.

### Full intermarket divergence detector

`intermarket/divergence.py` (expanded from Phase 2 basic version):
Nifty up + VIX up → fragile rally. Banks falling + Nifty flat → internal weakness.
Rupee strengthening + FII selling → contradiction (RBI intervention?). 
Crude rising + energy stocks falling → sector-specific problem.
Gold + equities both rising → liquidity flood, not fundamentals.

Divergence → reduce all long confidence by 10% for the session + emit divergence warning.

### Confidence calibration

`calibration.py`:
Bucket signals by confidence (0.55–0.65, 0.65–0.75, etc.).
Compare each bucket's actual win rate from paper_trades outcomes.
Are signals scored 0.80 winning 80% of the time?
Adjust layer weights if calibration is systematically off.

This is the first empirical feedback loop — confidence numbers must earn their meaning.

### Message template engine

`message_builder.py`:
Templates for each alert type (see Message Design Standard above).
Explainability: list top 3 contributing factors to confidence in every alert.
Historical odds section (from signal_outcomes, once 90+ days of data exist).

Risk and sizing enforcement in paper simulation:
- Structure/ATR stops (tighter of the two)
- Chandelier trail (highest_high − 3×ATR for longs)
- Scale-out: 40% at T1 (1R), trail 60% with chandelier to T2 (2R)
- Quarter-to-half Kelly, capped at 2% account risk per trade
- Daily kill-switches: −2% day = hard stop; 3 consecutive losses = pause half-size;
  5 consecutive losses = stop for day
- Volatility gross scaling: cut all gross exposure 40% when VIX > 22

### EOD summary

`eod_summary.py` (18:00 IST):
Market performance, sector leadership, day's signals breakdown, strategy health,
overnight events to watch (pending ratings, results), tomorrow's known catalysts.

