## Phase 10 — ML Enhancement (Month 12+)

**Goal:** Layer a learned model on top of the rules to catch what hand-coded rules cannot —
strictly after data readiness is confirmed.

### Data readiness gate (non-negotiable)

Before any training:
- ≥ 500 labeled examples per signal type (for each type you want to train)
- Multi-regime coverage (not all samples from one market condition)
- Point-in-time correct features (shift(1) verified throughout)
- Full cost model applied to all labels

If any gate fails: keep collecting. Do not proceed.

### Triple-barrier labeling

For each signal: upper barrier (TP = entry + 2×ATR), lower barrier (SL = entry − 1×ATR),
vertical barrier (15:20 IST forced flat).
Label: +1 if upper hit first, −1 if lower hit first, 0 if time barrier hit.
Dynamic σ_t (intraday 20-bar realized vol) makes labels heteroscedasticity-aware.

Uniqueness-of-label weighting: overlapping labels share information — down-weight proportionally.
Return-attribution weighting: weight by magnitude of return at barrier.

### Validation (CPCV only — no shortcuts)

Combinatorial Purged CV with purge horizon = max label span, embargo buffer after each segment.
Deflated Sharpe + PBO reported alongside raw Sharpe.
Walk-forward as sanity check only, never as primary validator.

### Models

**LightGBM** per signal type — one model per type, never a mega-model.
Logistic regression baseline on top features (sanity check — must beat this to be useful).
Sector-conditional heads only if data demands (not pre-split).

**Earnings drift (PEAD) model:** dedicated signal class for post-result drift.
Features: surprise vs prior, Day-0 reaction, gap behavior, delivery ratio.
Indian PEAD is well-documented and underexploited at retail.

**Exit intelligence model:** separate from entry. Predicts {hold, partial, trail, full-exit}
per bar given open position's MAE/MFE/regime context. More valuable than entry optimization.

### Meta-labeling

Rule engine decides side. Secondary LightGBM decides size.
Secondary model input: all features at signal time.
Secondary output: P(trade profitable | features).
Take trade only if calibrated P > 0.55.

Final confidence:
```
0.60 × rule_confidence + 0.40 × model_probability
```

Model adjusts size, never side. This is the correct use of ML in this system.

### Calibration + drift monitoring

Isotonic regression on OOS CPCV predictions to calibrate raw probabilities.
PSI/KS per feature weekly. Rolling 30-trade hit rate, profit factor, rolling Sharpe.
Challenger model in shadow mode 2 weeks before promotion.
Monthly minimum retraining; PSI breach triggers immediate retrain.

**Phase 10 exit criteria:**
- At least one signal type has a validated model beating its rules baseline net of costs
- Deployed as a size-adjusting secondary scorer
- Drift monitoring running and alerting

